<title>GERMANY: German imports of New Zealand lamb up sharply.</title>
<headline>German imports of New Zealand lamb up sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>German imports of New Zealand lamb jumped 42 percent in 1996 as beef consumption dived as a result of the mad cow disease crisis, the New Zealand Lamb information office here said.</p>
<p>A statement from the office said the trend was seen continuing this year as the latest outbreaks of swine fever discouraged consumption of locally produced pork.</p>
<p>Lamb imports from New Zealand in 1996 were 26,700 tonnes (18,800 in 1995) and those of sheep meat 6,300 (6,200).</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
